{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אבוא אליך", :translit "avo eilekha", :gloss "I will come to you"} {:he "אבוא", :translit "avo", :gloss "I will come"} {:he "אבוא אליך", :translit "avo eilekha", :gloss "I will come to you"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אבוא", :b "עולה עשרה לו'"} {:kind :other, :note "Ten men in synagogue is a minyan for public prayer (Berakhot 47b); the י may echo the ten of אבוא (1+2+6+1=10) as a sign of divine presence arriving when a quorum assembles."}], :frame {:text "The verse states 'אבוא אליך' — 'I will come to you.' Ba'al HaTurim links this to the concept of a minyan: when ten gather, the Divine Presence is said to be present among them, as in Pirkei Avot 3:6. The idea that י equals ten reinforces this: ten is the minimum count for a quorum that enables certain blessings and prayers, per Berakhot 47b. The comment envisions God saying: if you assemble י — a quorum of ten — in the synagogue, then 'I will come to you and bless you.'", :sources ["Pirkei Avot 3:6" "Berakhot 47b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "אבוא", :a-value 10, :b "עולה עשרה לו'", :b-value 722, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Ten men in synagogue is a minyan for public prayer (Berakhot 47b); the י may echo the ten of אבוא (1+2+6+1=10) as a sign of divine presence arriving when a quorum assembles.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:17:45.652456363Z", :model "glm-5.2"}